What this solution actually does: HotScan is a request-driven Windows service that screens payment operations against two compliance analyzers, FCM and the UT/Sentinel connector, before the payment engine continues, and that returns the incoming payments that the screening rejects. It does not poll. The dispatcher (General/Despachador) sends a TCP package with a list of long folios and an operation type to the port registered for the service; the host accepts clients on the loopback address only, with five concurrent clients by default (ServiceHost.cs:124 (../../General/HotScan/HotScan/ServiceHost.cs#L124), WindowsTcpServiceHostBase.cs:20-27 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Core/Estructura/WindowsTcpServiceHostBase.cs#L20-L27)), and hands each package to ProcesaFolios (ServiceHost.cs:130-141 (../../General/HotScan/HotScan/ServiceHost.cs#L130-L141), OperacionServicio.cs:148-171 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L148-L171)). For each folio the service reads the last pending process alias from the plan tables and runs up to four routes in sequence: (1) DATOS_GRAL marks the start of the HotScan step and, for the payroll and pay-and-pay types, the master folio (OperacionServicio.cs:221-256 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L221-L256)); (2) HOTSCAN/FCM runs the active analyzers through the orchestrator (OperacionServicio.cs:258-424 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L258-L424), LogicaOrquestador.cs:53-218 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Servicios/LogicaOrquestador.cs#L53-L218)): the FCM analyzer builds an XML request and inserts it into TBL_FCM_INTERCAMBIO for the FCM connector (LogicaFcm.cs:164-203 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Servicios/LogicaFcm.cs#L164-L203)), and the UT analyzer builds a screening request and posts it over HTTP with a bearer token (LogicaUtc.cs:120-190 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Servicios/LogicaUtc.cs#L120-L190), ClienteConectorUt.cs:45-120 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Servicios/ClienteConectorUt.cs#L45-L120)); (3) HOTSCAN_ESTATUS/FCM_ESTATUS reads the FCM and Sentinel answers and decides whether to reject and cancel, approve, hold or fail (OperacionServicio.cs:426-744 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L426-L744)), and a rejected incoming SPEI, SPEI_2, SPID or TEF operation is returned to the sender with a digitally signed record (OperacionServicio.cs:908-1111 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L908-L1111), CertificadoOperacion.cs:24-68 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Utileria/CertificadoOperacion.cs#L24-L68)), with reason code 14 after the SPEI cut-off hour and 2 otherwise (OperacionServicio.cs:1059-1062 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L1059-L1062)); (4) HOTSCAN_TERMINADO/FCM_TERMINADO updates the future-dated plan rows and closes the process (OperacionServicio.cs:746-779 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L746-L779)). The state lives in the TOMI database (RepositorioTomi.cs:25-27 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L25-L27)), which the service reads and writes through the 41 stored procedures of the database project, and the signed returns are written to the SPEI1, SPEI2, SPID and TEF databases (RepositorioSpeiUno.cs:18 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioSpeiUno.cs#L18), RepositorioSpeiDos.cs:19 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioSpeiDos.cs#L19), RepositorioSpid.cs:18 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioSpid.cs#L18), RepositorioTef.cs:16 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioTef.cs#L16)).
