False-positive checks were resolved as follows:
• No XML injection path exists in the FCM request: the three free-text fields go through Comunes.TextoBESS, which normalizes them and removes the characters in CaracterInvalido, including <, >, & and quotes (LogicaFcm.cs:113-122 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Servicios/LogicaFcm.cs#L113-L122), Comunes.cs:117-124 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Legacy/Comunes.cs#L117-L124), Comunes.cs:234-237 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Legacy/Comunes.cs#L234-L237)), and the payload is parsed with a DTD-prohibiting reader before it is written (LogicaFcm.cs:331-349 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Servicios/LogicaFcm.cs#L331-L349), XmlHelper.cs:150-175 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Infraestructura/XML/XmlHelper.cs#L150-L175)); the culture-dependent amount is a separate defect (HS-FR-12).
• The money bytes of the signature are culture-robust: DoubleToLong removes both . and , from the formatted amount (MetodosComunes.cs:309-343 (../../General/HotScan/Aplicacion/Utileria/MetodosComunes.cs#L309-L343)), so the culture finding is limited to the screening and FCM requests (HS-FR-12).
• The status-route lookups do not dereference a null alias: the shared ObtenerUltimoProceso returns an empty string when nothing is pending (RepositorioMaestro.cs:1372-1390 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Infraestructura/Repositorios/DBs/RepositorioMaestro.cs#L1372-L1390)); the empty string aborts the packet instead (HS-FR-6).
• A database failure does not silently disable FCM through the parameter loader: ObtenerParametrosHotScan throws when the whole list is empty (RepositorioTomi.cs:641-659 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L641-L659)); only a missing or mistyped row does (HS-FR-8).
• The analyzers do not dereference a null row: the repository throws for an empty result (RepositorioTomi.cs:1094-1121 (../../General/HotScan/Infraestructura/Servicio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L1094-L1121)), which also makes the "no data" branches dead (HS-FR-28).
• Convert.ToInt64(strFolio) cannot fail on a real folio, because the string is produced from a long; the two int conversions are a latent overflow only (HS-FR-30).
• No credential literal is present in the reviewed tree; the one in history is HS-FR-38. The service name set by the designer never runs (ServiceHost.cs:41 (../../General/HotScan/HotScan/ServiceHost.cs#L41)).
• The procedure and parameter names used by the C# all exist in the database project (GEN-13 does not apply); the parameter comparison differs only by the commented-out outputs (HS-FR-41).
Items that need business or owner confirmation before the corresponding fix is finalized:
• The meaning of the Sentinel status NA (not applicable, or "answer not written yet"), and whether any operation type is meant to be released when Sentinel is not active (HS-FR-3).
• Which operation types the dispatcher actually sends to HotScan, in particular SPID2, and whether ENT_COAS, FXT, TEF_Local and the other shared types are meant to be screened (HS-FR-16).
• Whether ENT_SPEI_2 returns are meant to read their data from the SPEI1 database (HS-FR-15), and the semantics of reason codes 2 and 14 and of the SPEI cut-off hour (HS-FR-1).
• The UT connector contract: https, token lifetime, the credential form (an unsalted SHA-256 of the stored value), the field length limits and whether TB_HotScan_General_Config holds the raw credentials (HS-FR-5, HS-FR-11, HS-FR-12).
• Whether automatic analyzer shutdown is wanted and the unit of AnalizerAutomaticReactivationTimeSec (HS-FR-10).
• Whether the exchange tables can hold more than one row per folio and type (HS-FR-27), and how the controller uses the status column of tb_srv_controladoradeservicios (HS-FR-6).
• The real unit of TamanoMaximoArchivoLogKB in the central configuration (HS-FR-32).
• Whether the certificate path and password in HotScanPruebasUnitarias/UnitTest1.cs were ever valid values (HS-FR-38).
• Whether the constants 'BBVA', '5990040' and 'MUFG' in the UT group-3 query are intended (HS-FR-41) and whether the legacy signature procedure left op_concepto_pag2, op_ref_numerica and the user key unassigned on purpose (HS-FR-40).
